      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Brother Island [zone=1017]\n**Who:**\n- Quigley Barnables [npc=47713]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Brother Island: The Cover of Night [zone=1026]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Brother Saldar [npc=48396]\n- Brother Sprudd [npc=48397]\n- Captain Sedgethwait [npc=48398]\n- Dabner Drednever [npc=48399]\n- Dagda Icefury [npc=48400]\n- Jameswell Dagmire [npc=48401]\n- Quigley Barnables [npc=48402]\n- a chest - The Cover of Night [npc=48687]\n- a siren seeker [npc=48393]\n- a siren slasher [npc=48394]\n- a siren snatcher [npc=48395]\n**Related Quests:**\n- TDS Progression #0: An Overview [quest=7701]\n- TDS Progression #6: Just Recompense [quest=7708]\n- TDS Progression #8: Loyal is the Heart [quest=7710]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 02:54:18 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This shared task (1-6 players) begins with Quigley Barnables ( **click for map image**) in the tower on Brother Island._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Completion of \"A Rising Storm\" (Tempest Temple)\n\\- Completion of \"Gathering Clouds\" (Tempest Temple)\n\\- Completion of \"Clearer Skies\" (Tempest Temple)\n\\- Completion of \"The Edge of Balance\" (Katta Castrum: Deluge)\n\\- Completion of \"The Abscent Scholar\" (Katta Castrum: Deluge)\n\\- Completion of \"Just Recompense\" (Brother Island)\n_Pre-Requisites for Participating:_\n\\- None\n_Say \"sleep\" to request the task and \"bed\" to zone into the instanced zone._\n_At the end of the previous task, you saw:_\nQuigley Barnables crosses his arms and furrows his brow. 'It's a good start, but a day's worth of deliveries can't repay a sack of gold! You're going to be here a long time if you think menial labor is going to return Firiona and her companions to my good graces!' Quigley laughs. 'You better get some [sleep]; you're going to have a long day ahead of you!'\nYou say, 'Hail, Quigley Barnables'\nQuigley Barnables says 'Why don't you go to [sleep] already?!'\nYou say, 'Sleep? Me?'\nQuigley Barnables says 'Yes, you should lie down. Starting tomorrow, I'll turn your sweat into gold, no matter what it takes! Get to [bed]!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Cover of Night'.\nDagda wants to use the cover of night to escape the island. If there is little trouble with sirens, this will be an easy escape.\nYou say, 'Bed, yes...'\nQuigley Barnables says 'Wake up ready to work!'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\n\n---\n\n!\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Dagda about getting off the island 0/2 (Brother Island)\n_Inside the instance, hail Dagda until the task updates._\nDagda Icefury laughs. 'Do you see blood on my sword? I didn't kill them! Not that I didn't want to, but the sirens got to them first.' Dagda holds out her thumb and forefinger. 'This close to battle for the first time in a while, and someone steals my kills!'\nDagda Icefury points down the beach. 'Have you spoken to Dabner and Sedgethwait? We need to... ' Dagda's voice is drowned out by a song flowing from the sea. She shouts to be heard as sirens creep up the beach. 'Salt and blood go well together. Finally my sword will be sated!'\n_At this time, 3x \"a siren seeker\" spawn and wander up to Dagda Icefury's location. They do not see invis._\n\n---\n\nKill the sirens 0/3 (Brother Island)\n_These are splittable, mezzable, and stunnable. They are Enchanter mobs and of average difficulty for Brother Island (hit for a max ~13,000). Upon the last death, you see:_\nThe sirens' song grows louder.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Dagda 0/2 (Brother Island)\n_Hail her until the task updates._\nDagda Icefury flings the blood off her sword with a snap of her wrist. 'You never forget the moves; you only lose the speed. But as long as these stay strong --' Dagda points to her head and then her heart -- 'this will remain strong.' Dagda raises her sword.\nDagda Icefury says 'We must warn Sedgethwait, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. He's our passage off this prison, and I know his men were never ones to resist the charms of beautiful women. Let's find him before we have to crew the Swift Fin ourselves!'\n\n---\n\nHead to Captain Sedgethwait 0/1 (Brother Island)\n_Location update - Captain Sedgethwait is found in the same place as in the non-instanced zone (the inlet on the east-central coast of the island). He is under some duress._\n\n---\n\nKill the sirens attacking Captain Dedgethwait 0/5 (Brother Island)\n_Kill 3x \"a siren seeker\" (as before) and 2x \"a siren snatcher\". These are all, again, straightforward and fairly simple to split. The snatchers hit a bit harder (~16,000) and seem to be Warrior class mobs._\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Captain Sedgethwait 0/1 (Brother Island)\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Sedgethwait'\nCaptain Sedgethwait says 'Half my crew... on the seas for months without women... they never stood a chance...' Sedgethwait stuffs the feathers more tightly in his ears. 'I saw a group of sirens heading for the dome!'\n\n---\n\nHead to the main building 0/1 (Brother Island)\n_Location update - the tower in the southern part of the zone, where you'll find another problem._\n\n---\n\nDefeat the sirens attacking Quigley and Saldar 0/10 (Brother Island)\n_Kill 4x \"a siren snatcher\" (as before) and 6x \"a siren slasher\" (hit for a max ~12,000; AE rampage; lots of hitpoints; mezzable; immune to stuns)._\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Quigley 0/5 (Brother Island)\n_Hail him until the task updates._\n**TASK LOCKS HERE**\nQuigley Barnables glares at Dagda. 'Too many brothers have already been carried off. They took Jameswell and Sprudd. The sirens were heading to the eastern beach!'\nDagda Icefury shouts 'And what of Dabner?'\nQuigley Barnables shouts 'The sirens can have him! What did he do to pay back our gold? Eat our food? Read our books? He was taken with the others, and good riddance!'\nDagda Icefury shouts 'If a siren could even stomach you, I'd feed you to them myself!' Dagda slashes at the nearby vegetation. 'Dabner will never be able to resist a siren's song! I've seen how easily he becomes attached. I always thought he should break his obsession, but I didn't want it to happen this way!'\nDagda Icefury says 'To the beach! We cannot leave our brothers to this fate!'\n\n---\n\nRescue Brother Sprudd from the sirens 0/4 (Brother Island)\n_Head due east to the coast, and kill 3x \"a siren snatcher\" 1x \"a siren slasher\" (as before)._\nBrother Sprudd shouts 'No, my pretty ladies!'\n\n---\n\nSave Jameswell from the sirens 0/5 (Brother Island)\n_Just next to the area is Jameswell Dagmire. Kill 3x \"a siren snatcher\" 2x \"a siren slasher\" (as before)._\nJameswell Dagmire runs toward Dagda, eyes wide and unseeing. 'My love, my beauty, you are the siren that has captured my heart! There is no other that can compare with you, Dagda!'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Jameswell 0/3 (Brother Island)\n_Hail him until the task updates._\nJameswell Dagmire staggers around, trying to shake the fog from his head. 'Are you... real? Or just another siren?' He reaches out his hand, trying to grab Dagda.\nDagda Icefury aims her sword at Jameswell's good arm. 'Easy there... you don't want to lose that one too!'\nQuigley Barnables points beyond the shore. 'Look, out in the water: It's the barbarian's toy, Dabner!'\n_A drowning Dabner Drednever flounders about offshore._\n\n---\n\nWait for Dagda to reach Dabner 0/1 (Brother Island)\nDagda Icefury cups her hands to her mouth. 'Dabner, it's Dagda! Swim back! I'm not a siren!'\nDabner Drednever's voice replies faintly, sounding hollow, wounded, and exhausted. 'I must follow the beauty. So much beauty out there, everywhere, all over Norrath... beauty I can hold... beauty less distant... beauty less cold...' Scaly hands rise out of the sea and pull Dabner into the depths.\nDagda Icefury rushes into the waves, not bothering to remove her armor. 'Dabner!'\nDagda Icefury shouts back to the shore, 'I'm going to find him!' Dagda disappears into the sea.\n_Both of them disappear into the sea..._\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Quigley 0/5 (Brother Island)\n_Hail him until the task completes. A chest also spawns at this time. The task is repeatable with a 6-hour lockout timer from the time of request._\nQuigley Barnables groans. 'Don't be stupid. It would be suicide to follow her in the dark underwater! You'd never find the cavern entrance!'\nJameswell Dagmire shouts 'I'll go! When daylight comes I'll follow Dagda into the deepest darkness of the sea!'\nQuigley Barnables shouts 'You're not going anywhere! Look at yourself all wide-eyed and panting! You're not fit to be anywhere near women!'\nQuigley Barnables wipes his brow and looks at you. 'This could be the chance for you and Firiona's companions to redeem themselves. I lost many brothers tonight, and many more have already been taken. If you can rescue them, the debt is forgiven. I've already sent Horace the Resolved to the caverns, but as of yet I've heard nothing from him. Perhaps you won't fail.\nQuigley Barnables says 'At first light I will send Brother Dilgen and Brother Visius to the caverns. Meet them there, and together bring back my brothers!' Quigley blows his nose on his kerchief. 'If you fail, I can always see how much the Swift Fin can fetch at the Barren Coast.'\n_Rewards:_\n150 platinum\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 item + 0-1 armor templates + 0-1 Briny Essences + 0-1 Valiant ornament):_\nConch of Singing Seas\nDagger of Sinister Waters\nLost Light of the House\nMask of Stormy Seas\nSailor's Lucky Coin\nTideworn Armguards\nTideworn Boots\nTideworn Bracer\nTideworn Gloves\nTideworn Helm\nTideworn Leggings\nTideworn Tunic\nLesser Briny Essence\nMedian Briny Essence\nGreater Briny Essence\n- Conch of Singing Seas [item=118758]\n- Dagger of Sinister Waters [item=120620]\n- Lost Light of the House [item=119542]\n- Mask of Stormy Seas [item=121750]\n- Sailor's Lucky Coin [item=120686]\n- Tideworn Armguards [item=120797]\n- Tideworn Boots [item=120646]\n- Tideworn Bracer [item=120702]\n- Tideworn Gloves [item=120685]\n- Tideworn Helm [item=119785]\n- Tideworn Leggings [item=120798]\n- Tideworn Tunic [item=120681]",
